Z||000006||theogre||05-22-2001||10:19 AM||||It sounds like you are running into a few problems...... Not all of it is Fiero related.<P>Allot of good shops don't like to install unknown used parts in any car. Been there, done that... It causes more problems than it solves allot of the time. And yes, part markup has something to do with it, but it's not all of it. Used parts can really eat huge amounts of time. You'd be amazed the stuppid ____ that can go wrong that takes hours to fix.<P>Also, allot of shops don't like to do engine swaps and transmission work at all if they can avoid it. These usually arean't jobs they can simply push out of the way if there's a hold up. Once it's in the bay, it's there untill completion. This can cause big problems in little shops with only a few bays. A stalled job could leave them short a lift for days.<P>Now add in that most shops simply can't grasp that Fiero Powertrain is simply an FWD system moved back a few feet....<P>In this case you are asking them to tie up a lift for at least 3 days right up front. Assuming they don't have a bunch of broken/stripped bolts... It will take 1 day to strip the parts, then 1 day each at least to get the parts into the respective cars. This will also tie up 2 mechanics for a big part of the time.<P>labor charge wise, you may not save much, if anything on the tranny vs them supplying one. The engine job is a toss up.||||reg||1
Z||000007||skitime||05-22-2001||12:49 PM||||theogre, Thanks for that perspective that I know I had not thought of.  Luckily I can do most of the work myself but at least I will be more understanding when I do get a bill.  Good insight.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Topknot||05-22-2001||03:28 PM||||Hallo fldevel,<P>Well I live in Orlando Florida, not to sure how far from you I am, but if close enuff I might find a few weekends to pop by and assist.<P>But I do see a few heavy duty work loads on your list.  To be moving complete engine and tranny swaps also requires the associated hardware and computer items.  So full tear downs are in order.  Also do you have the space to location to have parts laying out for a day or so while the work is being done.<P>Like here at my house I'm in the process of doing a clutch replacement..(Also nursing a broken Pinky Finger..see my postings lol)  And the City doesn't like car parts laying around for too many days..<P>Topknot =]<BR>||||reg||1
